# =============================================================================
# Rockdale County Motivated Seller Scraper
# =============================================================================
# Two kinds of files live in data/: results you want kept forever, and working
# files that would either bloat the repository or break the push outright.
# The rules below separate them. See the note at the bottom for the files that
# are deliberately NOT ignored -- ignoring those would quietly break features.
# =============================================================================

# --- The parcel cache. This one matters. ------------------------------------
# The scraper can download a whole county parcel roll and
# keeps it here so it does not have to re-download daily. That file is roughly
# 140 MB. GitHub refuses any single file over 100 MB, so committing it would
# not merely bloat the repo -- it would make every push fail with an error that
# is very hard to undo once the file is in your history.
# GitHub Actions caches this between runs instead, so nothing is lost.
data/.cache/
*.cache/

# --- Half-written files -----------------------------------------------------
# The scraper writes to a .tmp file first and renames it into place, so that a
# crash mid-write cannot corrupt your lead list. If it is killed at exactly the
# wrong moment a stray .tmp is left behind; it should never be committed.
*.tmp
*.bak

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.Python
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Playwright / browsers ---------------------------------------------------
# The Chromium binary is ~150 MB and is installed fresh (or restored from the
# Actions cache) on every run.
ms-playwright/
.playwright/
playwright-report/
test-results/
node_modules/

# --- Credentials -------------------------------------------------------------
# Your GoHighLevel key belongs in GitHub Secrets, never in a file in the repo.
# A public repository makes any key committed here visible to everyone, and
# deleting it later does not remove it from the history.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json
secrets.json

# --- Editors and operating systems -------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- Logs --------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/

# =============================================================================
# DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED
# =============================================================================
# These sit in data/ and look like working files, but each one has to be
# committed or a feature stops working. GitHub Actions runners are wiped after
# every run, so anything not committed is gone by the next morning.
#
#   data/records.json                    your lead list
#   dashboard/records.json               what the dashboard reads
#   data/ghl_leads.csv                   your CRM import file
#   dashboard/ghl_leads.csv              the copy the dashboard links to
#
#   data/seen_documents.json             remembers which documents have been
#                                        seen before. Without it, every lead
#                                        looks brand new every morning and the
#                                        "New this week" flag becomes useless.
#
#   data/landmark_learned_selectors.json how the scraper taught itself to
#                                        operate the Clerk's website. Without
#                                        it, it relearns the site from scratch
#                                        daily instead of going straight to
#                                        what already worked.
#
#   data/unmapped_doc_types.json         document types the scraper did not
#                                        recognize, so the list can be grown
#                                        from real DeKalb data.
#
#   data/landmark_discovery.json         diagnostics written only when the
#   data/landmark_failure.png            Clerk's site changes. Keeping them in
#   data/landmark_page_dump.html         the repo means you can send them
#                                        straight from GitHub instead of
#                                        digging through workflow artifacts.
#
#   NEEDS_ATTENTION.md                   plain-English note that appears only
#                                        when something needs a human. Deletes
#                                        itself once the problem clears.
# =============================================================================
